course: dictionary
lesson: 2711
title: Making it weaker
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To dilute something is to make it weaker or thinner, usually by adding water or another liquid. Squash that tastes too strong needs more water. Dilute can be a verb, as in «dilute the squash», or an adjective, as in «a dilute acid».
explain: «Squash is a solution: more water makes it more dilute, and a sieve or filter cannot take the cordial back out.» The clue is more water. Adding water makes the squash weaker, so dilute means weaker. Once the water is mixed in, you cannot pull it back out with a sieve.
explain: The word can also mean making something less strong in effect. To dilute the message means to make it less strong, so it hits less hard. Check by swapping in your meaning: does «make the message weaker» still make sense in the sentence? If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Dilute can be a verb (dilute, dilutes, diluted, diluting) or an adjective (dilute).
fact: To dilute a liquid means to make it weaker or thinner by adding water or another liquid.
fact: «A dilute acid» means an acid that has had water added, so it is weaker.
fact: In science, a dilute solution has less of the dissolved substance in the same amount of water.
fact: Labels that say «dilute before use» mean you should add water or another liquid before you use the product.
exercise: «Squash is a solution: more water makes it more dilute.» What does dilute mean here? | *Weaker, because water has been added | Frozen solid | Stronger, because sugar has been added | Cold and fizzy
exercise: A bottle label says «dilute before use». What should you do? | Shake it hard and open it | Drink it straight from the bottle | *Add water or another liquid before you use it | Keep it in the freezer until winter
exercise: Which phrase means to make a message less strong? | Print the message in bold | Shout the message | *Dilute the message | Repeat the message
test: «A dilute acid» is an acid that is: | Stronger, because more acid was added | Sweeter and safer to drink | *Weaker than before, because water was added | Hotter than before
test: In «grey, which is a "diluted" black», what does diluted suggest? | Darker than black | *Lighter, a weaker version of black | Spotted with white patches | Shiny and smooth
exam: Choose the meaning that best fits "to dilute": | *To make something weaker by adding water or another liquid | To freeze something solid | To mix two colours together to make a new one | To make something stronger by heating it
